Z||000027||Patrick's Dad||10-26-2000||11:21 AM||||jhogans, at a guess, I'd say $8-12K new, not including the mods to match it with the N*, but it's the only manual xaxle I can think of that could handle that kind of power (except for the Italians, but that means spinning the engine 90 deg.)<P>Lincoln's LS's do have a V8 option, but no manual. At the moment, I am anti FoMoCo, as my wife owns an Exlorer that leaks oil and ATF (propper maintenance notwithstanding) and has a door that sags more than 1" below the opening. Ford has shrugged me off at all levels. I don't know about you guys, but I have a 13 year old Pontiac with bigger, heavier doors that never had such a problem. My 27 yo Plymouth, too.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
